{"id":"DRKS00025138","src":"drks","title":"European disease registry on Retinopathy of Prematurity (ROP)","official":"","summary":"The EU-ROP registry is a European wide multicenter non-interventional observational registry study intended to run open-ended in as many countries as possible including infants treated for retinopathy of prematurity irrespective of the used treatment modality. The registry is strictly observational; only clinical routine data is collected, no study-specific examinations or interventions are to be performed.","conditions":["Retinopathy of prematurity"],"interventions":[{"type":"ARM","name":"Baseline demographic data, treatment data, and follow-up information will be collected on patients treated for ROP independent of the type of treatment. Both the number of study centers as well as the number of patients to be included into the registry are not limited."}],"criteria":"Inclusion criteria:\nROP requiring treatment according to the respective national ROP screening and treatment guidelines\nExclusion criteria:\nDenial or absence of consent for documentation and storage of personal data by parents or legal guardians","minAge":"","maxAge":"","sex":"ALL","healthy":false,"studyType":"OBSERVATIONAL","purpose":"","enrollment":null,"start":"2021-08-06","pcd":"","upd":"2026-11-02","sponsor":"Universitätsklinikum Greifswald","areas":["other","rare"],"central":["Professor Dr. Andreas Stahl · Universitätsklinikum Greifswald · +49 383486 5900 · andreas.stahl@med.uni-greifswald.de"],"sites":[{"f":"Ernst von Bergmann Klinikum","city":"Potsdam","zip":"","s":"R","pr":"","c":"","lat":52.3989,"lon":13.0657},{"f":"Department for Ophthalmology","city":"Paris","zip":"","s":"R","pr":"","c":"","lat":52.5164,"lon":13.3787},{"f":"Helios Klinikum","city":"Berlin","zip":"","s":"R","pr":"","c":"","lat":52.5244,"lon":13.4105},{"f":"Vivantes Klinikum","city":"Berlin","zip":"","s":"R","pr":"","c":"","lat":52.5244,"lon":13.4105},{"f":"St. Franziskus Klinik","city":"Münst